<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
      Deliberately empty.

      This plugin declares no permissions. READ_PHONE_STATE is a runtime
      permission that shows up in the Play Console and obliges the app to file
      a data-safety declaration, so it is the app's decision to make, not the
      package's. Apps that only need the permission-free subset (network
      operator, SIM state, MCC/MNC of the active SIM) never have to ask for
      anything.

      To read per-SIM data, declare this in your own app's manifest:
        <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_PHONE_STATE" />

      Separately, TelephonyManager.isDataEnabled() accepts ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE
      rather than READ_PHONE_STATE. That one is an install-time permission with
      no prompt, so an app that wants the cellular-data state but not per-SIM
      data can declare only:
        <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />
    -->
</manifest>
